{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Anti-MRSA, Synergistic AMPs", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of defensin 1 shows 50.7% similarity to insect Tenecin 1. Activity: E. coli Active against S. aureus MW2, USA100, USA300, USA400, RN4220, Newman, and clinical isolates including BF1,BF5, BF7 to BF11 and S. epidermidis 9142 (MIC 16-64 ug/ml). Of the 23 AMPs tested, only this peptide is effective against S. pneumoniae D39 ( Lindhauer et al., 2019). Synergy:AMPs: It showed synergistic effects with telavancin (synergy2) and daptomycin (synergy1). Antimicrobial robustness: Activity can be compromised by salts: NaCl-sensitive:S. aureus MW2 (50-100 mM); CaCl2-sensitive:S. aureus MW2 (1.25-100 mM). Animal model:Caenorhabditis elegans: it showed dose-dependent protection of animal survival against MRSA. Updated 10/2019; 4/2025", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "26062137", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2015 Jun 10;10(6):e0128576. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02579", "source_id": "AP02579", "source_numeric_id": "02579", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02579", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "A Defensin from the Model Beetle Tribolium castaneum Acts Synergistically with Telavancin and Daptomycin against Multidrug Resistant Staphylococcus aureus", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
